+  // in place is a `Defn.Define`'s instructions (a method BODY edit) where
+  // that method's owning Top's class hierarchy, attrs, and full member-
+  // signature set are byte-identical to what this instance was already
+  // built from. Anything else it can't prove safe -- a changed Var/Const/
+  // Declare, an added/removed/re-signatured member, a changed parent/
+  // traits/attrs, a Top that disappeared, changed entry points/service
+  // providers, changed `config`/`entries`, or a lingering unreachable/
+  // unsupported failure from the last build -- makes it return `None`, and
+  // the caller falls back to a completely fresh `Reach` (today's behavior,
