+  // cache (patches/scala-native-0043, `incremental-reach` branch) wasn't:
+  // that attempt tried to *replay* memoized edges/call-targets/allocation
+  // facts without re-running the worklist at all, which silently dropped
+  // targets whenever the cache missed a fact kind (the documented
+  // Function1.apply miscompile). This instead *re-runs* the real worklist
+  // (`process()`/`processDelayed()`) over the changed bodies, so every
+  // ordinary reach rule (reachOp/reachMethodTargets/reachAllocation/dynamic
+  // dispatch registration/...) still executes exactly as it does for a
+  // fresh build -- nothing is memoized or replayed, only *skipped* for
+  // Tops that provably can't have produced new reachability facts. And
+  // because every one of those rules only ever ADDS to `done`/`infos`/
+  // `dyncandidates`/`dynimpls`/responds maps (never removes), a stale fact
+  // left over from a method body that changed to no longer need something
